y in stroke patients.", "MODIFIED MANN ASSESSMENT OF SWALLOWING:The Modified Mann Assessment of Swallowing is a screening tool used to identify patients with dysphagia and refer them for further evaluation.", "ST. LOUIS:St. Louis is a city in Missouri, home to Barnes-Jewish Hospital and known for its medical facilities.", "PATIENCE:The patient is the individual undergoing assessment for swallowing capabilities and reactions to stimuli.", "SUITER:Suiter is an author referenced in the document, known for research on dysphagia and swallowing assessments.", "LEDER:Leder is an author referenced in the document, known for contributions to the study of dysphagia.", "JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NURSING:The Journal of Clinical Nursing is a publication where Perry's work on swallowing assessments was published.", "DYSHPHAGIA:Dysphagia refers to difficulty in swallowing, which is the primary focus of the assessments described in the document.", "ARCHIVES OF NEUROLOGY:The \"Archives of Neurology\" is a scholarly publication that focuses on studies related to various neurological conditions, including dementia and cognitive decline. Additionally, it serves as a platform for research on swallowing and dysphagia, as evidenced by a publication from DePippo. This journal encompasses a wide range of topics within the field of neurology, contributing to the understanding and treatment of neurological disorders.", "PERRY:", "DEPIPPO:", "BELAFSKY:Belafsky is a researcher who validated the Eating Assessment Tool-10 (EAT-10) in 2008.", "DRA. R. BURGOS:Dra. R. Burgos is a researcher who translated the EAT-10 into Spanish and contributed to its validation."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}